resh. All of the drop comes from orders, and AOV did not change. Web and android each lost 201,600 EUR (87.5% down), while iOS did not move. Within orders, the drop is all checkout conversion: cart_to_checkout_rate on web and android fell from 0.5 to 0.0625, starting at 03:00Z. That is exactly when checkout-web v5.8 was released, unplanned and scoped to web and android. Discovery reports 7,168 TypeErrors tagged v5.8 on the checkout page on each of web and android, and none on iOS, which uses a native checkout. Payment success held at 0.9375 everywhere, which rules out the PSP-2 latency problem. The android v9.14 release came 2 hours before the drop and web fell just as much without it, so it is not the cause. The planned Black Friday campaign should have raised GMV by 35%, not lowered it.", "verdict": "CONFIRMED"}, "name": "submit", "toolset_name": null, "type": "tool_use"}], "context_management": null, "diagnostics": null, "id": "msg_011ChGHAb7a1mzGP1BGXa9yt", "input_transformations": null, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 6984, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 10153, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 6984, "input_tokens": 10153, "model": null, "output_tokens": 2956, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 2956, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}}
